{"id":"gun-parts","rev":1,"lang":"en","status":"published","review_flag":null,"disclaimer":null,"title":"Parts of the gun","summary":"Stock, action, fore-end, barrels, rib and chokes: the names of the main parts of an over-and-under, so you can follow a coach or a gunsmith in Sporting™ and Compak® Sporting.","body":[{"k":"gear-gun-parts-p1","t":"p","html":"Coaches name the parts of the gun all the time, so learn them from the shoulder to the muzzle of an <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/over-and-under/\">over-and-under</a>, the most common competition gun. The <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/stock/\">stock</a> goes into the shoulder. Its top edge, where the cheek rests, is the <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/comb/\">comb</a>; 'raise the comb' or 'drop the comb' is about <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/gun-fit/\">gun fit</a>. The narrow part held by the trigger hand is the <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/grip/\">grip</a>, and the rubber pad at the end is the <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/recoil-pad/\">recoil pad</a>.","disc":null,"rule_ref":null,"anchor":"gear-gun-parts"},{"k":"dg-gun-parts","t":"diagram","html":"<figure class=\"dg\" aria-labelledby=\"dg-gun-parts\"><p class=\"dg-h\" id=\"dg-gun-parts\">The parts of an over-and-under</p><svg class=\"dg-svg\" viewBox=\"0 30 760 220\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"dg-gun-parts\" focusable=\"false\"><path class=\"dg-pad\" d=\"M30 94h14v96h-14z\"/>\n<path class=\"dg-wood\" d=\"M44 92 L215 112 Q238 116 252 122 L262 140 L250 160 Q228 156 205 151 L44 190 Z\"/>\n<path class=\"dg-wood\" d=\"M340 141 H462 Q474 141 474 150 Q474 159 462 159 H352 Q340 159 340 150 Z\"/>\n<rect class=\"dg-metal\" x=\"252\" y=\"108\" width=\"86\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\"/>\n<path class=\"dg-steel\" d=\"M264 104h12v6h-12z\"/><path class=\"dg-steel\" d=\"M300 100 h30 v8 h-30z\"/>\n<path class=\"dg-guard\" d=\"M262 160 Q262 192 284 192 Q306 192 306 160\"/><path class=\"dg-steel-l\" d=\"M282 160 q4 14 -2 22\"/>\n<rect class=\"dg-steel\" x=\"338\" y=\"112\" width=\"392\" height=\"13\" rx=\"2\"/><rect class=\"dg-steel\" x=\"338\" y=\"127\" width=\"392\" height=\"13\" rx=\"2\"/>\n<path class=\"dg-rib\" d=\"M338 109 H730\"/><circle class=\"dg-bead\" cx=\"727\" cy=\"105\" r=\"3.5\"/>\n<path class=\"dg-choke\" d=\"M708 112v28\"/><path class=\"dg-ld\" d=\"M120 228L120 160\"/><circle class=\"dg-ldd\" cx=\"120\" cy=\"160\" r=\"3\"/><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"228\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"228\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">1</text></g><path class=\"dg-ld\" d=\"M130 54L130 104\"/><circle class=\"dg-ldd\" cx=\"130\" cy=\"104\" r=\"3\"/><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"54\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"54\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">2</text></g><path class=\"dg-ld\" d=\"M232 228L236 150\"/><circle class=\"dg-ldd\" cx=\"236\" cy=\"150\" r=\"3\"/><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"232\" cy=\"228\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"232\" y=\"228\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">3</text></g><path class=\"dg-ld\" d=\"M37 228L37 180\"/><circle class=\"dg-ldd\" cx=\"37\" cy=\"180\" r=\"3\"/><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"37\" cy=\"228\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"37\" y=\"228\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">4</text></g><path class=\"dg-ld\" d=\"M330 228L320 152\"/><circle class=\"dg-ldd\" cx=\"320\" cy=\"152\" r=\"3\"/><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"228\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"228\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">5</text></g><path class=\"dg-ld\" d=\"M318 54L318 100\"/><circle class=\"dg-ldd\" cx=\"318\" cy=\"100\" r=\"3\"/><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"318\" cy=\"54\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"54\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">6</text></g><path class=\"dg-ld\" d=\"M262 54L270 104\"/><circle class=\"dg-ldd\" cx=\"270\" cy=\"104\" r=\"3\"/><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"262\" cy=\"54\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"262\" y=\"54\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">7</text></g><path class=\"dg-ld\" d=\"M284 228L284 190\"/><circle class=\"dg-ldd\" cx=\"284\" cy=\"190\" r=\"3\"/><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"284\" cy=\"228\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"284\" y=\"228\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">8</text></g><path class=\"dg-ld\" d=\"M405 228L405 158\"/><circle class=\"dg-ldd\" cx=\"405\" cy=\"158\" r=\"3\"/><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"405\" cy=\"228\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"405\" y=\"228\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">9</text></g><path class=\"dg-ld\" d=\"M560 228L560 139\"/><circle class=\"dg-ldd\" cx=\"560\" cy=\"139\" r=\"3\"/><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"560\" cy=\"228\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"560\" y=\"228\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">10</text></g><path class=\"dg-ld\" d=\"M600 54L600 109\"/><circle class=\"dg-ldd\" cx=\"600\" cy=\"109\" r=\"3\"/><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"600\" cy=\"54\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"600\" y=\"54\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">11</text></g><path class=\"dg-ld\" d=\"M727 54L727 101\"/><circle class=\"dg-ldd\" cx=\"727\" cy=\"101\" r=\"3\"/><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"727\" cy=\"54\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"727\" y=\"54\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">12</text></g><path class=\"dg-ld\" d=\"M716 228L720 136\"/><circle class=\"dg-ldd\" cx=\"720\" cy=\"136\" r=\"3\"/><g class=\"dg-n\"><circle cx=\"716\" cy=\"228\" r=\"14\"/><text x=\"716\" y=\"228\" text-anchor=\"middle\" dominant-baseline=\"central\">13</text></g></svg><ol class=\"dg-leg\"><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">1</b>Stock</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">2</b>Comb (the cheek rests here)</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">3</b>Grip</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">4</b>Recoil pad</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">5</b>Receiver (action)</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">6</b>Top lever: push it aside and the gun opens</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">7</b>Safety catch, often with the barrel selector</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">8</b>Trigger, in its guard</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">9</b>Fore-end</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">10</b>Barrels</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">11</b>Rib</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">12</b>Bead: a reference, not a sight</li><li><b aria-hidden=\"true\">13</b>Muzzle, where the chokes are screwed in</li></ol><figcaption>From the shoulder to the muzzle: the names coaches use all the time.</figcaption></figure>","disc":null,"rule_ref":null},{"k":"gun-parts-p2","t":"p","html":"The stock is made of wood or a composite material. The recoil pad softens the push of the shot, and pads or spacers of different thickness change the length of the stock.","disc":null,"rule_ref":null},{"k":"gear-gun-parts-p2","t":"p","html":"The metal centre of the gun is the <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/receiver/\">receiver</a> or action. On top sits the <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/top-lever/\">top lever</a>: push it aside and the gun opens. Behind it is the <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/safety-catch/\">safety catch</a>, often combined with the <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/barrel-selector/\">barrel selector</a>, which decides which barrel fires first. Underneath is the <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/trigger/\">trigger</a> in its guard.","disc":null,"rule_ref":null},{"k":"gun-parts-p4","t":"p","html":"Inside the receiver sits the firing mechanism. Most competition over-and-unders have a single trigger for both barrels.","disc":null,"rule_ref":null},{"k":"gear-gun-parts-p3","t":"p","html":"A release trigger fires when it is let go, not when it is pressed. Such a gun must carry, as a warning, a sticker with a large 'R' on a fluorescent background on the outer side of the stock.","disc":"both","rule_ref":null},{"k":"gear-gun-parts-p4","t":"p","html":"Under the barrels the other hand holds the <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/fore-end/\">fore-end</a>. The <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/barrel/\">barrels</a> have <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/chamber/\">chambers</a> at the back for the cartridges and <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/muzzle/\">muzzles</a> at the front, where <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/choke/\">chokes</a> are screwed in. Along the top runs the <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/rib/\">rib</a> with a <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/bead/\">bead</a> at the end. The bead is a reference, not a sight: 'look at the target, not the bead'.","disc":null,"rule_ref":null},{"k":"gun-parts-p5","t":"p","html":"The fore-end also holds the barrels on the action: take it off, and the barrels come off. That is how a gun is taken apart for cleaning and transport. The rib usually has gaps underneath (a 'ventilated rib'), so that heat from the barrels makes the air above it shimmer less. Many guns have a small mid bead halfway along the rib.","disc":null,"rule_ref":null},{"k":"gun-parts-p7","t":"p","html":"Next to the chambers sit the <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/ejector/\">ejectors</a>: when the gun is opened, they throw out the fired cases. Simpler extractors only lift the cases a little, and you take them out by hand.","disc":null,"rule_ref":null},{"k":"gear-gun-parts-p5","t":"warn","html":"One safety rule is linked to the parts. After a misfire or any other gun or cartridge <a class=\"term\" href=\"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/malfunction/\">failure</a>, the shooter does not open the gun or touch the safety until the referee has looked at it.","disc":"both","rule_ref":null}],"notes":[{"k":"gun-parts-n1","for":"interpreter","html":"Two false friends: the 'rib' is the strip along the top of the barrels, and 'break the gun' means open it on its hinge, not damage it."}],"phrases":[{"k":"gear-gun-parts-ph1","speaker":"coach","en":"You're seeing too much rib — your head is up.","meaning":"The eye is too high above the rib, usually because the head lifts off the comb.","say":null,"audio":1},{"k":"gear-gun-parts-ph2","speaker":"coach","en":"Check your selector — you fired the top barrel first.","meaning":"The barrel selector is set the wrong way round.","say":null,"audio":1},{"k":"gear-gun-parts-ph3","speaker":"coach","en":"Break your gun and show me it's clear.","meaning":"Open the gun and show empty chambers.","say":null,"audio":1},{"k":"gear-gun-parts-ph4","speaker":"coach","en":"Forget the bead — look at the target.","meaning":"Focus on the target, not on the end of the barrel.","say":null,"audio":1}],"key_points":[{"k":"gear-gun-parts-kp1","html":"Stock, comb, grip, recoil pad; receiver with top lever, safety and selector; trigger.","checklist":false},{"k":"gear-gun-parts-kp2","html":"Fore-end, barrels with chambers and muzzles, rib with bead.","checklist":false},{"k":"gear-gun-parts-kp3","html":"A release trigger needs an 'R' sticker on the stock.","checklist":false},{"k":"gear-gun-parts-kp4","html":"'Break the gun' means open it; the rib is the strip along the top of the barrels.","checklist":false},{"k":"gear-gun-parts-kp5","html":"After a misfire: do not open the gun or touch the safety before the referee checks.","checklist":true}],"did_you_know":{"k":"gun-parts-dyk","html":"Selective ejectors throw out only a fired case. If you fired one barrel, the unfired cartridge in the other is only lifted a little, so you can take it out calmly by hand."},"quiz":[{"k":"gear-gun-parts-q1","q":"A coach says 'Raise the comb'. Which part does he mean?","options":[{"k":"a","text":"The top of the stock, where the cheek rests"},{"k":"b","text":"The small bead at the end of the rib"},{"k":"c","text":"The guard around the trigger"},{"k":"d","text":"The choke tube at the muzzle"}],"correct":"a","explain":"The comb is the top of the stock; raising it lifts the eye above the rib."},{"k":"gear-gun-parts-q2","q":"What must a gun with a release trigger carry?","options":[{"k":"a","text":"A red-painted barrel to warn others"},{"k":"b","text":"A large 'R' sticker on the stock"},{"k":"c","text":"A second, separate safety catch"},{"k":"d","text":"Nothing: no marking is required"}],"correct":"b","explain":"Both rulebooks require the 'R' warning sticker, on a fluorescent background, on the outer side of the buttstock.","rule_ref":"sporting:ch7-release-trigger-marking","disc":"both"},{"k":"gun-parts-q1","q":"What is the barrel selector for?","options":[{"k":"a","text":"To take the barrels off the action"},{"k":"b","text":"To change the choke in the barrel"},{"k":"c","text":"To throw the fired cases out"},{"k":"d","text":"To choose which barrel fires first"}],"correct":"d","explain":"The selector, often combined with the safety, sets the order of the barrels."}],"terms":[{"id":"gunsmith","en":"Gunsmith","local":"","label":"Gunsmith","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/gunsmith/"},{"id":"shotgun","en":"Shotgun","local":"","label":"Shotgun","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/shotgun/"},{"id":"over-and-under","en":"Over-and-under","local":"","label":"Over-and-under","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/over-and-under/"},{"id":"stock","en":"Stock","local":"","label":"Stock","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/stock/"},{"id":"comb","en":"Comb","local":"","label":"Comb","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/comb/"},{"id":"grip","en":"Grip","local":"","label":"Grip","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/grip/"},{"id":"recoil-pad","en":"Recoil pad","local":"","label":"Recoil pad","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/recoil-pad/"},{"id":"receiver","en":"Receiver","local":"","label":"Receiver","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/receiver/"},{"id":"top-lever","en":"Top lever","local":"","label":"Top lever","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/top-lever/"},{"id":"safety-catch","en":"Safety catch","local":"","label":"Safety catch","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/safety-catch/"},{"id":"barrel-selector","en":"Barrel selector","local":"","label":"Barrel selector","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/barrel-selector/"},{"id":"trigger","en":"Trigger","local":"","label":"Trigger","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/trigger/"},{"id":"release-trigger","en":"Release trigger","local":"","label":"Release trigger","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/release-trigger/"},{"id":"fore-end","en":"Fore-end","local":"","label":"Fore-end","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/fore-end/"},{"id":"barrel","en":"Barrel","local":"","label":"Barrel","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/barrel/"},{"id":"chamber","en":"Chamber","local":"","label":"Chamber","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/chamber/"},{"id":"muzzle","en":"Muzzle","local":"","label":"Muzzle","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/muzzle/"},{"id":"choke","en":"Choke","local":"","label":"Choke","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/choke/"},{"id":"rib","en":"Rib","local":"","label":"Rib","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/rib/"},{"id":"bead","en":"Bead","local":"","label":"Bead","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/bead/"},{"id":"ejector","en":"Ejector","local":"","label":"Ejector","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/ejector/"},{"id":"gun-fit","en":"Gun fit","local":"","label":"Gun fit","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/gun-fit/"},{"id":"malfunction","en":"Malfunction","local":"","label":"Malfunction","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/en/glossary/malfunction/"}],"rule_refs":[{"book":"sporting","id":"ch7-release-trigger-marking","label":"Chapter 7 · Release trigger: mandatory 'R' sticker","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/rules/en/sporting/weapons-and-ammunition/#ch7-release-trigger-marking"},{"book":"compak","id":"ch18-release-trigger-marking","label":"Chapter 18 · Release trigger: the 'R' sticker","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/rules/en/compak/shooting-equipment/#ch18-release-trigger-marking"},{"book":"sporting","id":"ch8-malfunction-stay-put","label":"Chapter 8 · After a misfire: do not open the gun","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/rules/en/sporting/rules-of-conduct-safety/#ch8-malfunction-stay-put"},{"book":"compak","id":"ch24-malfunction-zero","label":"Chapter 24 · Malfunction: opening before inspection costs the target","url":"https://juliabezdolna.github.io/clayaway/rules/en/compak/safety-rules/#ch24-malfunction-zero"}],"sources":[{"title":"FITASC — official rules of Parcours de Chasse – Sporting™ and Compak® Sporting","url":"https://www.fitasc.com/disciplines-sportives/reglements-sportifs","fitasc":true}],"evidence":[],"more_in_en":0}
